    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19215" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">galbĭnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		either from galbanum or from GALBUS, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>greenish-yellow</i>, <i>yellowish;</i> cf. tunica,
				<i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 34</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">avis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 68, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cingillum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 67, 4</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst. plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">galbĭna</span></b>  (sc.
			vestimenta), ōrum, n., <i>pale-green garments</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 2,
			97</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>effeminate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					1, 97, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
